  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Development and implementation of a National Strategy for Quality Infrastructure (ENIQ) for Brazil</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Ministry of Development, Industry, Trade and Services (MDIC) approached UNIDO to provide technical guidance for the development of a National Strategy of Quality Infrastructure (ENIQ). The ENIQ will cover a period of 10 years, and is expected to be launched by December 2024, following the publication of a draft version, a public consultation and submission to the National Council of Metrology, Standardization and Industrial Quality (Conmetro) for its approval by November 2024.  The engagement with UNIDO began in early 2024 with a three-month period of Preparatory Assistance (PA). The PA had two objectives: First, to finalize this definitive project document (ProDoc) for the intervention to develop the ENIQ over the course of 2024, along with the elaboration of a methodology and work plan for the first stages of its implementation over the 2024 # 2026 timeframe.  The ENIQ, with a 10-year horizon, will include an Implementation Plan and biennial Action Plans to guide its deployment, which is expected to start in 2025. It will build on Brazil#s experiences with its existing, mature, QI and focus on ways in which this needs to evolve and improve in line with the country#s overall development strategies. The Implementation and associated Action Plans will articulate the activities foreseen for the various key st</narrative>
  </description>
